  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Who owns the task?",
      "items": [
        "Pueue schedules the task. The guardian owns its lifetime; delegate-run starts the provider and captures its output.",
        "Fresh preflight runs before provider Start. Scope closure precedes sealing and publication."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Where is the answer?",
      "items": [
        "TaskDir evaluates sealed evidence and commits outcome.json. That record establishes the terminal verdict.",
        "The lead uses status, logs and collect to observe the same task; collection does not request another provider turn."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Optional workspace capture",
      "items": [
        "Managed Git isolation adds a checkout and independent capture receipts; it does not change the provider's task outcome.",
        "Workspace helpers reuse the supervised task path. The lead reviews the capture and explicitly releases the retained checkout."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Refusal, stopping and continuation",
      "items": [
        "Confirmed resource pressure refuses a fresh task before task creation. An unavailable metric alone warns rather than refuses.",
        "Cancellation records a stop request for an active task; cancel on a terminal task returns without changing it (internal/tasklifecycle/cancel.go:13–41).",
        "Eligible continuation creates a linked successor in the caller's scope with the recorded provider session; predecessor records stay unchanged (internal/tasklifecycle/continue.go:10–90)."
      ]
    }
  ]
